From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:10:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a style-only resolve, start web-font fetches from it and
 reshape only what a font changes

A computed-value reader needs resolved styles but no box tree, and re-resolving layout for one
answer costs a whole pass over the document. Add a resolve that restyles and stops before layout,
and answer the computed-value reads from it.

A style-only pass also sees a font face it has never registered. Start the fetch there so the font
is in flight while the box tree is being built, rather than after the first layout that needs it.

A web font arriving after the first layout damaged every inline layout in the document, so a face
used by one table on html.spec.whatwg.org cost a full 740k-node relayout. Only text whose
font-family names the registered family can shape differently; reshape those inline roots and the
inline roots above them. A face with no family name still reshapes everything. The damage is
applied at the next resolve rather than on each delivery, so a page that receives N faces walks its
nodes once instead of N times.
